LadybugDB bundles third-party components under permissive licenses, including
MIT, BSD, Apache License 2.0, and dual MIT/Apache License 2.0 terms. Copyright
notices and the complete license texts supplied by each component are retained
in tools/vendor/ladybugdb-0.20.4.tar.xz in the source package. They include the
license files for ALP, ANTLR4, Brotli, cppjieba/limonp, FastPFOR, LZ4, Mbed TLS,
miniz, Parquet/Thrift, PCG, pybind11, RE2, CRoaring, SimSIMD, Snappy, spdlog,
taywee/args, utf8proc, yyjson, and Zstandard.

{fmt} 9.1.0, bundled with spdlog in that archive, is compiled into the package
on toolchains whose C++ library cannot provide std::format, such as the older
Apple clang releases on some CRAN macOS machines.

